      "symbols": [
        {
          "docstring": "Topics are GitHub's own tag system. Up to **20** per repo. They are not decoration: `github.com/topics/<topic>` is a real, crawlable, ranked page, and",
          "lines": [
            15,
            50
          ],
          "name": "Where it moved: repo TOPICS",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "| surface | limit | why it is indexed | |---|---|---| | repo **description** | ~350 chars | shown in every search result and every org listing; the si",
          "lines": [
            51,
            58
          ],
          "name": "The other three legitimate surfaces",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "**This works, and it was measured rather than argued.** One call to GitHub's own markdown renderer (`POST https://api.github.com/markdown`, HTTP 200)",
          "lines": [
            59,
            101
          ],
          "name": "The signature block \u2014 the forum trick, ported verbatim",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "**A \"META injector\" cannot inject meta tags into a GitHub page** \u2014 row 1 of the table above. `<meta>` is deleted before the page is served, so no craw",
          "lines": [
            102,
            111
          ],
          "name": "What does NOT work, measured rather than assumed",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "A bot whose job is to bump a timestamp so the repo *looks* updated is **inauthentic activity** under GitHub's Acceptable Use Policies, and enforcement",
          "lines": [
            112,
            125
          ],
          "name": "What would actively cost us the repo",
          "type": "section"
        },
        {
          "docstring": "`.github/workflows/verify.yml` runs **every Monday**. It re-proves the whole packet against whatever Lean and mathlib currently are, then writes the r",
          "lines": [
            126,
            143
          ],
          "name": "What we ship instead, which produces the same visible effect honestly",
          "type": "section"
        }
      ]
